    "summary": "Smoky Passenger, debut Tiger guitar; solid second set despite mix",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a smoking Passenger and an expansive Playing In The Band that lift the second set. Jerry debuts his custom “Tiger” guitar with strong tone, while Brent shines on Althea and Shakedown Street. Mix is muddied in the soundboard source, but the performance remains compelling.",
    "review": "August 4 1979 at the Oakland Auditorium Arena finds the Dead rolling into a fresh era of songs with confidence. The first set showcases new material—Althea, Lost Sailor and a jaunty Deal—but it’s the second set that truly shines: Passenger roars, Shakedown Street grooves into a soaring Playing In The Band, and the band rides an expansive jam through Drums, Space and a soulful Stella Blue before closing with Sugar Magnolia. Jerry’s long‑awaited “Tiger” guitar makes its debut on Althea and again on Passenger, offering a bright, cutting tone that many reviewers called “sweetest Garcia.” Brent Mydland is front‑and‑center in the mix, delivering crisp keyboards on Shakedown Street and adding depth to Althea. While the soundboard tape is noted as muddy—vocals sometimes buried and a brief glitch—the musical chemistry outweighs the technical flaws, making this a must‑listen performance for fans of the late‑‘70s era.\n\nThe audience recordings capture the same energy with clearer ambience but lack the detail of the SBD source. Overall, the show stands as a solid entry in the 1979 catalog: strong song choices, a noteworthy guitar debut, and tight rhythm section work, even if the mix occasionally clouds the nuance.",
